      <h2>2. Sage HR</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Workforce scheduling, leave management, and HR compliance</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.4 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £4/user/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Sage HR brings order to the chaos of care worker scheduling. A care provider in Sheffield with 80 staff uses it to manage rotas, track leave, and ensure compliance with Working Time Regulations. The AI features predict staffing shortages based on historical absence patterns, suggest optimal shift patterns, and flag workers approaching overtime limits before they breach them.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI-powered scheduling:</strong> Generate optimised rotas that balance staff preferences, skill requirements, and labour cost targets.</li>
        <li><strong>Absence prediction:</strong> Machine learning analyses historical absence data and predicts likely sick days, suggesting cover in advance.</li>
        <li><strong>Leave management:</strong> Self-service holiday requests with automatic approval workflows and clash detection.</li>
        <li><strong>Timesheets and clock-in:</strong> GPS-verified clock-in via mobile app. Ensure carers arrive at the right location at the right time.</li>
        <li><strong>Compliance tracking:</strong> Automatic alerts for training expiry dates, DBS renewal deadlines, and mandatory certification requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Payroll integration:</strong> Seamless connection with Sage Payroll and third-party providers. Reduce payroll processing from days to hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Shift swapping:</strong> Carers swap shifts through the app with manager approval, reducing last-minute no-shows.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £4/user/month, it is affordable even for small care providers</li>
        <li>The absence prediction feature reduced unplanned leave by 23% for one Nottingham provider</li>
        <li>GPS clock-in provides evidence of visit attendance for CQC and local authority audits</li>
        <li>Compliance tracking prevents the last-minute panic of expired training certificates</li>
        <li>The mobile app is intuitive. Carers with limited tech experience use it without training</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The AI scheduling is good but not perfect. Complex rotas with multiple constraints still need human oversight</li>
        <li>Integration with non-Sage payroll systems requires setup time and sometimes middleware</li>
        <li>The interface feels dated compared to newer HR platforms like Personio or HiBob</li>
        <li>Customer support is primarily email-based on the lower tiers. Phone support costs extra</li>
        <li>Some users report occasional sync delays between the mobile app and the web dashboard</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate Sage HR 4.3/5 for ease of use. A Capterra reviewer from a Liverpool care home said the absence prediction "changed our staffing from reactive to proactive." The main complaint across review sites: the mobile app lacks some features available on the desktop version, forcing managers back to their desks.</p>

