      <h2>3. Nuance Dragon Medical One</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Clinical documentation, voice-enabled note taking, and GP integration</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.6 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £90/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Nuance Dragon Medical One is the industry standard for voice-driven clinical documentation. A GP practice in Bristol uses it to dictate patient notes directly into EMIS Web, reducing documentation time from 2 hours per day to 30 minutes. The AI understands medical terminology, drug names, and regional accents with remarkable accuracy, learning each clinician's speech patterns over time.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Medical speech recognition:</strong> Understands 90+ medical specialties with vocabulary covering drugs, procedures, and anatomy. Accuracy exceeds 99% after voice profile training.</li>
        <li><strong>EMIS and SystmOne integration:</strong> Dictate directly into the UK's major GP clinical systems. No copy-paste, no transcription errors.</li>
        <li><strong>Ambient clinical intelligence:</strong> Automatically generates structured clinical notes from natural patient-clinician conversations. Reduces after-hours documentation by up to 70%.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile app:</strong> Dictate notes on ward rounds, home visits, or between appointments. Syncs with the desktop application.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom commands:</strong> Create voice shortcuts for repetitive phrases. "Insert standard asthma review" expands to a full template.</li>
        <li><strong>Secure cloud storage:</strong> NHS-compliant data handling with encryption at rest and in transit.</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-language support:</strong> Dictate in English, Welsh, or switch between languages mid-session for bilingual practices.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The most accurate medical speech recognition available. Outperforms generic tools like Otter.ai for clinical terminology</li>
        <li>EMIS integration means notes flow directly into patient records without manual transfer</li>
