      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI candidate screening:</strong> Automatically parse CVs and rank candidates against job requirements. Identify qualified applicants in seconds, not hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Compliance automation:</strong> Track DBS status, right-to-work documents, training certificates, and qualification expiry dates. Receive alerts before anything lapses.</li>
        <li><strong>Interview scheduling:</strong> Automated calendar integration that finds mutually available slots without the email ping-pong.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate communication:</strong> Automated email and SMS updates keep applicants informed at every stage. Reduce ghosting and improve candidate experience.</li>
        <li><strong>Pipeline analytics:</strong> See where candidates drop out of your process and why. Optimise your funnel for conversion.</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-posting:</strong> Advertise roles across NHS Jobs, Indeed, LinkedIn, and specialist healthcare boards from one interface.</li>
        <li><strong>Reference checking:</strong> Automated reference requests with structured responses. Compare referees' ratings across standardised criteria.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The compliance automation is essential for healthcare. One agency reduced DBS expiry incidents by 94%</li>
        <li>AI screening saves 15-20 hours per week for active recruiters</li>
        <li>Multi-posting means no more copy-pasting job descriptions across five different sites</li>
        <li>The candidate experience is professional. Applicants receive updates promptly, improving your employer brand</li>
        <li>Pipeline analytics reveal bottlenecks. One client discovered their interview scheduling delay was losing 30% of qualified candidates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £149/month, it is an investment for small agencies recruiting fewer than 20 roles per month</li>
        <li>The AI screening occasionally misses context. A candidate with non-traditional experience may score poorly despite being ideal</li>
        <li>Integration with NHS Jobs and some specialist boards requires manual setup</li>
        <li>The interface has a learning curve. Expect 2-3 weeks before your team is fully productive</li>
        <li>Customer support is good but primarily UK business hours, which can frustrate international candidates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
