      <h2>8. Tableau</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Healthcare analytics, performance dashboards, and strategic reporting</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.5 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £60/user/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Tableau transforms the data that healthcare providers collect into actionable insights. A care home group in Scotland uses it to visualise occupancy trends, staff turnover rates, complaint categories, and financial performance on a single dashboard. The AI features (Tableau Einstein) suggest questions you should ask of your data, automatically generate explanations for anomalies, and predict future trends based on historical patterns.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Drag-and-drop analytics:</strong> Build sophisticated dashboards without coding. Connect to Birdie, Sage HR, Radar Healthcare, and dozens of other healthcare platforms.</li>
        <li><strong>AI-powered insights:</strong> Tableau Einstein automatically surfaces trends, outliers, and correlations. "Your falls rate increased 15% in Wing B but not Wing A. The difference? Wing B has 20% more agency staff."</li>
        <li><strong>Predictive analytics:</strong> Forecast occupancy, staffing needs, and cash flow based on historical data and seasonal patterns.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile dashboards:</strong> Access key metrics on tablet or smartphone. CQC inspectors can view real-time compliance data during visits.</li>
        <li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Share dashboards with board members, regulators, and operational staff. Control who sees what with row-level security.</li>
        <li><strong>Natural language queries:</strong> Ask questions in plain English. "Show me medication errors by shift and carer tenure" generates the visualisation instantly.</li>
        <li><strong>Embedded analytics:</strong> Integrate dashboards into your existing care management platforms for seamless workflow.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The most powerful visual analytics platform available. Handles millions of rows without slowing down</li>
        <li>AI insights reveal patterns that spreadsheet analysis misses. One provider discovered their highest-rated carers had the lowest training completion rates</li>
        <li>Natural language queries make analytics accessible to non-technical managers</li>
        <li>Mobile dashboards mean you can check key metrics between site visits</li>
        <li>The healthcare community shares templates and best practices freely</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £60/user/month, it is expensive for small providers. The learning curve is steep</li>
        <li>Requires clean, structured data. If your current systems export messy spreadsheets, expect a data cleaning project first</li>
        <li>The AI insights are suggestive, not prescriptive. Human interpretation is still essential</li>
        <li>Some users report performance issues with very large datasets (100,000+ rows)</li>
        <li>Training requirements are significant. Budget for a Tableau course or consultant</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate Tableau 4.4/5, calling it "the gold standard for business intelligence." A Trustpilot reviewer from a Scottish care home group said the predictive analytics "transformed our planning from guesswork to data-driven decisions." The main complaint: the price excludes smaller providers who would benefit most from better analytics.</p>

